WEBVTT

00:01:33.980 --> 00:01:36.240
<b>Ride the Crab</b>

00:01:33.980 --> 00:01:36.240
<b>Ride the Crab</b>

00:01:42.230 --> 00:01:44.900
Whew, looks like no one's following us.

00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:47.330
Quit clinging to me over 
every little thing, dummy!

00:01:47.330 --> 00:01:49.490
I'm already wearing 
tons of layers as it is.

00:02:03.250 --> 00:02:06.180
Hey, Bisco, we're veering off-course.

00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:09.030
If we keep going this way, we'll miss 
the mark and end up too far east.

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:14.670
Don't say ill-omened things like 
"miss the mark" to an archer. You heathen.

00:02:14.670 --> 00:02:16.770
This is the problem with city brats.

00:02:16.770 --> 00:02:18.290
That's not the issue!

00:02:18.290 --> 00:02:21.530
Are we sure this is the right way? 
We didn't take the wrong path, did we?

00:02:21.530 --> 00:02:23.900
I've never been mistaken in my life.

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:27.170
Really? Because we're 
supposed to be going to Akita.

00:02:28.650 --> 00:02:32.080
What an annoying panda you are! 
Who do you think you're talkin' to here?!

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:34.300
Sheltered boys should 
just shut up and follow!

00:02:34.610 --> 00:02:38.040
Tsk. Now where'd that guy go off to?

00:02:52.660 --> 00:02:54.820
Look, Bisco, it's driftweed.

00:02:54.820 --> 00:02:57.700
I hear it absorbs light from
 the sun and glows at night.

00:02:57.700 --> 00:03:01.250
The rumors I heard about it in 
Imihama said it's a very pretty—

00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:04.190
Why're you being so carefree?

00:03:04.590 --> 00:03:06.240
You think we're sightseeing?! Come on!

00:03:06.570 --> 00:03:09.820
Th-That's not why I mentioned it.

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:13.590
When the driftweed glows at night, 
it attracts bugs and beasts.

00:03:13.590 --> 00:03:16.340
So I want to get through here
 while it's still daylight.

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:18.340
Let your guard down and you'll die.

00:03:19.170 --> 00:03:20.690
S-Sorry.

00:03:56.290 --> 00:03:57.050
Here.

00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:06.390
That's bitter!

00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:08.540
Don't chew it, dummy.

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:10.510
The guts of these little guys are bitter.

00:04:10.510 --> 00:04:13.560
You gotta swallow it in one gulp, head-first.

00:04:13.890 --> 00:04:15.690
Swallow it? This thing?!

00:04:15.690 --> 00:04:19.290
If you don't eat, you won't 
be able to walk. Again.

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:29.280
Hey, Bisco...

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:33.130
By my estimates, Pawoo's body 
should last about three months

00:04:33.130 --> 00:04:34.910
thanks to those mushroom injections.

00:04:35.510 --> 00:04:37.610
But the problem is Jabi-san...

00:04:38.410 --> 00:04:40.670
I think he has another month at best.

00:04:43.670 --> 00:04:49.160
Even if Jabi-san's right, and the Rust 
Eater is in a secluded part of Akita,

00:04:49.160 --> 00:04:51.330
there's no way we'll make it in time walking.

00:04:51.330 --> 00:04:54.940
But if we get a car and 
use the Imihama Highway,

00:04:54.940 --> 00:04:57.260
we'll be caught by the Watch in no time.

00:04:57.540 --> 00:05:00.970
You think I'm just some moron who's 
only good at fighting, don't you?

00:05:00.970 --> 00:05:02.890
I know all that.

00:05:03.390 --> 00:05:06.020
I didn't set out on this 
journey without a plan.

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:08.350
You have some kind of idea, then?

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:13.290
<b>Shimobuki</b>

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:15.160
<b>Ashio Bonecoal Mountains</b>

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:15.160
<b>Niigata</b>

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:15.160
<b>Tain</b>

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:15.160
<b>Gunma</b>

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:15.160
<b>Tochigi</b>

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:15.150
The tip of the Ashio Bonecoal Mountains 
extends to just north of here.

00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:20.470
In the mines there, the longest railcar line 
runs all the way to southern Yamagata.

00:05:20.830 --> 00:05:23.750
If we find a good connection there, 
it shouldn't even take two days.

00:05:23.750 --> 00:05:25.920
The Ashio mines?

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:28.690
You mean we're passing through 
the Bonecoal Mountains?!

00:05:32.060 --> 00:05:37.200
I heard the iron mice living in the Bonecoal
 Mountains are fierce and frightening.

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:41.810
They say, when the swarm attacks, a man can
 be reduced to bones in less than ten seconds.

00:05:41.810 --> 00:05:45.240
No matter how strong you are,
 the two of us can't...

00:05:48.300 --> 00:05:50.880
Who said it was only the two of us going?

00:05:50.880 --> 00:05:53.190
Huh? But who else is there?

00:05:53.190 --> 00:05:56.330
The third member of our party,
 well... I just found him.

00:06:02.850 --> 00:06:04.780
You dummy. He's on our side.

00:06:11.380 --> 00:06:15.250
Th-That's your... friend?

00:06:16.090 --> 00:06:17.300
My brother.

00:06:20.230 --> 00:06:22.610
This is Actagawa. He's a steelcrab.

00:06:22.610 --> 00:06:24.890
I had him go east, around the walls.

00:06:25.430 --> 00:06:30.030
He doesn't like the heat, so I figured he'd 
buried himself, and I was looking for him.

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:33.740
So that's why we went east...

00:06:34.710 --> 00:06:36.740
The animals lurking in the bonecoal mines

00:06:36.740 --> 00:06:40.310
never attack something they can't 
sink their teeth or poison into.

00:06:40.670 --> 00:06:44.970
Plus, this guy can walk through any terrain,
and he's stronger than heavy machinery.

00:06:53.240 --> 00:06:54.590
Amazing.

00:06:55.910 --> 00:06:58.090
I'm Nekoyanagi Milo.

00:06:58.090 --> 00:07:00.010
Nice to meet you, Actagawa.

00:07:06.100 --> 00:07:08.110
Actagawa, you idiot!

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:24.590
Wear that.

00:07:24.590 --> 00:07:26.000
I forgot that Actagawa...

00:07:26.270 --> 00:07:27.840
hates doctors.

00:07:31.880 --> 00:07:33.790
It suits you surprisingly well.

00:07:33.790 --> 00:07:34.820
Really?

00:07:34.820 --> 00:07:37.290
Only how it looks, I mean.

00:07:41.370 --> 00:07:43.610
It's okay, I'm not an enemy.

00:07:44.010 --> 00:07:45.280
I'm Milo.

00:07:45.620 --> 00:07:47.920
I'm Bisco's new partner.

00:07:51.950 --> 00:07:57.290
I'd like to travel with you and join 
Bisco in his search for the Rust Eater.

00:08:05.030 --> 00:08:06.220
<i>I managed to get on!</i>

00:08:10.540 --> 00:08:12.490
Ouch...

00:08:13.240 --> 00:08:16.460
So just yank on this here, 
and he'll whirl around.

00:08:16.460 --> 00:08:19.560
If Actagawa gets all excited and
 goes "Raaargh," just go "Hey!"

00:08:19.560 --> 00:08:22.330
Then thwap down hard like 
this to get him to stop.

00:08:19.930 --> 00:08:22.810
He's using more sound effects than words.
 I can barely understand him.

00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:26.960
Well, either way, once you understand how 
he feels, you won't need logic anymore.

00:08:27.760 --> 00:08:29.310
Want to give riding him a try?

00:08:29.310 --> 00:08:31.610
Yeah, I'll try it.

00:08:31.810 --> 00:08:34.720
All right, let's see what you've got.

00:08:37.070 --> 00:08:39.140
Here we go, Actagawa.

00:08:55.830 --> 00:08:58.600
Guess I didn't snap the reins right, huh?

00:08:58.600 --> 00:08:59.820
I'm sorry.

00:09:03.120 --> 00:09:05.680
You put too much power into the reins.

00:09:05.680 --> 00:09:08.360
There's no way you can 
match Actagawa's strength.

00:09:08.750 --> 00:09:11.320
No, not that way!

00:09:13.670 --> 00:09:14.350
Ow.

00:09:16.690 --> 00:09:19.400
If you're nice to him, he'll be nice to you, too.

00:09:19.400 --> 00:09:21.860
Try thinking about how Actagawa feels.

00:09:23.900 --> 00:09:24.930
Ow!

00:09:28.460 --> 00:09:29.660
He hates me.

00:09:32.700 --> 00:09:34.680
Don't sulk over that.

00:09:34.680 --> 00:09:38.390
If some crab you didn't know tried to 
ride you, you'd punch him, too, right?

00:09:40.230 --> 00:09:43.100
He's got his pride as a crab, too.

00:09:43.530 --> 00:09:45.350
You just have to get used to each other.

00:09:45.350 --> 00:09:50.350
But which will break first, 
his pride or the bones in my neck?

00:09:50.350 --> 00:09:52.880
You've always got something
 to say, don't ya, Panda?

00:09:53.380 --> 00:09:55.800
Actagawa's our trump card.

00:09:56.370 --> 00:09:58.700
You should make friends with him quickly.

00:09:58.910 --> 00:10:03.940
Then I'd like proper instruction 
instead of just idealism.

00:10:22.520 --> 00:10:26.470
<i>At this rate, it'll be impossible to
 get through Bonecoal Mountains.</i>

00:10:26.850 --> 00:10:30.230
<i>Holding Bisco back is the one 
thing I don't want to do.</i>

00:10:30.230 --> 00:10:31.720
<i>Actagawa, please!</i>

00:10:34.240 --> 00:10:35.770
<i>He's going too fast!</i>

00:10:37.850 --> 00:10:40.410
Actagawa! Stop!

00:10:52.030 --> 00:10:53.470
I'm sorry.

00:10:53.470 --> 00:10:55.520
You aren't hurt anywhere, are you?

00:10:57.440 --> 00:11:00.490
You know, that's one 
incredible crab you're riding.

00:11:08.780 --> 00:11:10.990
Yup, that should do it.

00:11:11.770 --> 00:11:15.310
Crab thief!

00:11:15.830 --> 00:11:20.070
Panda-kun, just give it 
up and let go already!

00:11:20.070 --> 00:11:22.300
What's that idiot doing?

00:11:32.830 --> 00:11:35.290
Hey, whose crab do you think 
you're layin' your hands on?!

00:11:35.290 --> 00:11:37.560
Want me to feed you to him?!

00:11:49.800 --> 00:11:53.560
You idiot. What did you even 
do to end up in that situation?

00:11:54.060 --> 00:11:55.310
I'm sorry.

00:11:55.720 --> 00:11:59.820
That girl said she'd show me 
the ropes, so I just... yeah.

00:12:00.660 --> 00:12:03.810
Okay, that's enough. 
We'll train again tomorrow.

00:12:11.200 --> 00:12:13.210
I'm sorry for pushing you too hard.

00:12:13.210 --> 00:12:15.320
I'm going to apply some medicine, 
so stay still, okay?

00:12:16.330 --> 00:12:17.580
Don't bother acting tough!

00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:21.510
Good, now sit.

00:12:23.720 --> 00:12:25.730
There. Good boy.

00:12:27.830 --> 00:12:32.590
Why can't you ride on his 
back when you can do this?

00:12:33.670 --> 00:12:36.100
Do this? Do what?

00:12:37.900 --> 00:12:39.160
Whatever.

00:12:39.160 --> 00:12:40.720
Change of plans.

00:12:40.720 --> 00:12:42.530
No more crab training.

00:12:42.530 --> 00:12:45.120
You've got talent when it comes to crabs.

00:12:45.120 --> 00:12:45.980
Huh?

00:12:46.300 --> 00:12:51.490
First time I've ever seen someone who could 
talk to a crab before they could ride it.

00:12:54.190 --> 00:12:57.880
This is far enough. 
We're almost at the Ashio Mountains.

00:12:59.460 --> 00:13:01.030
What's that?

00:13:03.410 --> 00:13:05.760
Okay, we'll sleep here for tonight.

00:13:05.760 --> 00:13:08.730
Make sure you heal your own wounds, too.

00:13:11.840 --> 00:13:13.760
Looks like someone beat us here.

00:13:14.350 --> 00:13:17.300
What's this? It's the crab thief from earlier.

00:13:19.770 --> 00:13:23.340
Hmm? Wait, now I remember.
 I saw you in Imihama, too.

00:13:23.340 --> 00:13:25.780
Did someone order you to follow—

00:13:27.850 --> 00:13:29.020
Bisco, move!

00:13:36.570 --> 00:13:38.560
There's something in her stomach.

00:13:38.560 --> 00:13:40.370
This'll be a bit rough, but...

00:13:52.650 --> 00:13:54.220
What's that thing?

00:13:54.220 --> 00:13:55.730
A balloonworm.

00:13:55.730 --> 00:13:59.560
It's a worm they used to use to 
prevent slaves from escaping.

00:13:59.560 --> 00:14:03.940
Feed the slave the egg, then drugs to stop it
from hatching. That way, they're yours for life.

00:14:03.940 --> 00:14:05.650
Nowadays, it's used on prisoners.

00:14:05.650 --> 00:14:09.270
You mean the Imihama governor's 
been using them on his special forces?

00:14:10.020 --> 00:14:13.550
No wonder they're always 
taking that strange medicine.

00:14:13.550 --> 00:14:15.370
That damn cheating governor!

00:14:15.370 --> 00:14:16.900
Here, drink some water.

00:14:17.180 --> 00:14:22.350
<i>I can't believe he can help someone 
who made a fool of him earlier in the day.</i>

00:14:23.170 --> 00:14:24.720
You saved me!

00:14:26.570 --> 00:14:28.260
A-A-A-Akaboshi?!

00:14:28.260 --> 00:14:29.670
Why are you here again?!

00:14:29.670 --> 00:14:34.190
Huh? Shouldn't "Thank you, great doctor!" 
be the first words out of your mouth instead?

00:14:35.200 --> 00:14:36.960
You must be joking.

00:14:36.960 --> 00:14:40.200
If you're saving a lone 
woman out on a journey,

00:14:40.200 --> 00:14:43.020
you must be looking for <i>that</i>, right?

00:14:44.010 --> 00:14:46.490
You did just give me
 the most incredible kiss.

00:14:46.490 --> 00:14:47.460
Huh?!

00:14:47.460 --> 00:14:49.410
That's not why I did that!

00:14:49.950 --> 00:14:51.430
How adorable.

00:14:51.430 --> 00:14:53.690
Hey, Doctor, that worm just now...

00:14:53.690 --> 00:14:57.450
I think there might still be 
another one in my stomach.

00:14:57.450 --> 00:14:59.480
Hey, cut that out already.

00:14:59.480 --> 00:15:03.450
Who'd get any pleasure out of putting
 their hands on that flat body of yours?

00:15:03.450 --> 00:15:06.380
So Akaboshi-kun's never 
been with a woman, huh?

00:15:06.380 --> 00:15:11.720
Hee hee! I guess even Man-Eating Akaboshi 
is an innocent virgin underneath.

00:15:13.200 --> 00:15:14.980
Calm down, Bisco!

00:15:14.980 --> 00:15:17.670
Hey, you're a peddler, right?

00:15:17.670 --> 00:15:20.240
We don't have enough food.

00:15:20.240 --> 00:15:22.860
If you don't mind, could 
you share some with us?

00:15:22.860 --> 00:15:26.600
You two really aren't after my body?

00:15:26.600 --> 00:15:29.640
Then why'd you save someone like me?

00:15:29.640 --> 00:15:34.250
If you wanted my goods, you could've 
just taken them after I died.

00:15:34.250 --> 00:15:35.860
Now that you mention it, that's true.

00:15:35.860 --> 00:15:39.250
I can't just stand by and let 
someone die right in front of me.

00:15:39.250 --> 00:15:40.380
Right, Bisco?

00:15:40.380 --> 00:15:45.110
Looks like I got rescued 
by a bona fide softie.

00:15:45.110 --> 00:15:47.610
I can't tell if that makes me lucky or pathetic.

00:15:47.610 --> 00:15:51.380
Well, whatever. In that case,
 I'll treat this as business.

00:15:53.870 --> 00:15:57.650
Welcome to the charming 
jellyfish shop, you two.

00:15:58.070 --> 00:15:59.630
Jellyfish shop?

00:15:59.630 --> 00:16:02.450
My hair looks like a jellyfish, right?

00:16:02.450 --> 00:16:05.310
We specialize in blueprints 
for weapons and arms,

00:16:05.310 --> 00:16:07.510
but we have plenty of food to offer, too.

00:16:07.510 --> 00:16:11.200
How about this 100% pure scorpion honey?

00:16:11.200 --> 00:16:13.020
It melts in your mouth!

00:16:13.020 --> 00:16:17.160
It just needs to fill our bellies.
Don't you have coal bread or salt mochi?

00:16:17.370 --> 00:16:20.150
We don't carry poor people food.

00:16:20.530 --> 00:16:21.810
Look, Bisco!

00:16:21.810 --> 00:16:23.910
She has butter-flavored Bisco cookies!

00:16:23.910 --> 00:16:26.290
Let's get these! You love them, right?

00:16:26.290 --> 00:16:28.930
Uh, well, I've never had them before.

00:16:28.930 --> 00:16:32.170
We Mushroom Keepers rarely 
ever get a hold of stuff like that.

00:16:32.360 --> 00:16:34.010
All the more reason to get them.

00:16:34.010 --> 00:16:36.050
So, um, can we have this?

00:16:36.050 --> 00:16:38.360
Huh? That's all you want?

00:16:38.360 --> 00:16:39.850
They're 4 sols a pop.

00:16:39.850 --> 00:16:43.560
Huh?! After all of that, you're charging us?!

00:16:43.560 --> 00:16:45.040
Of course I am!

00:16:45.040 --> 00:16:49.260
I lost out on your bounty because you 
just happened to be too strong for me!

00:16:49.260 --> 00:16:51.060
Don't go saying stingy stuff to me!

00:16:53.200 --> 00:16:55.250
Well, that was a boring sale.

00:16:55.250 --> 00:16:59.110
I'm going to sleep now. It's 100 sols
 if you touch me, you got that?

00:16:59.110 --> 00:17:01.840
Oh, half price for you, Panda-kun.

00:17:01.840 --> 00:17:04.060
Just go sleep already!

00:17:04.060 --> 00:17:07.180
Bisco, getting mad will 
just make you hungry.

00:17:06.210 --> 00:17:07.920
<b>BISCO</b>

00:17:15.920 --> 00:17:20.290
Well? How's your namesake? 
Different from what you imagined?

00:17:20.290 --> 00:17:25.470
I thought it'd be harder.
After all, the name means "strong."

00:17:25.470 --> 00:17:27.560
It's got a nourishing flavor, too.

00:17:27.560 --> 00:17:30.310
I thought it'd taste like a bear's liver.

00:17:30.910 --> 00:17:34.110
There's no way it would!
It's a sweet treat, after all.

00:17:34.110 --> 00:17:35.900
Well, was it good?

00:17:35.900 --> 00:17:37.460
Yeah, it was good.

00:17:37.990 --> 00:17:40.570
H-Hey, you're eating too many!

00:17:40.580 --> 00:17:41.990
I was saving mine!

00:17:41.700 --> 00:17:44.830
<b>Liquid Bonecoal</b>

00:17:41.990 --> 00:17:44.820
Well, I can't sell gas to a crab rider.

00:17:44.820 --> 00:17:46.970
This is old now, so I'll toss it.

00:18:01.110 --> 00:18:02.860
What's going on?!

00:18:02.860 --> 00:18:04.090
Hey, Milo, wake up!

00:18:14.100 --> 00:18:17.750
The War Memorial wasn't 
just used to purify weapons.

00:18:17.750 --> 00:18:20.330
The whole temple itself 
is an animal weapon!

00:18:20.870 --> 00:18:22.100
Help me!

00:18:22.100 --> 00:18:24.700
You dumbass, get off me!

00:18:24.700 --> 00:18:26.370
No, no! Don't leave me behind!

00:18:26.360 --> 00:18:29.420
Just how damn strong is this girl?!

00:18:27.670 --> 00:18:29.920
No way, no way, no way!

00:18:29.420 --> 00:18:30.750
Bisco!

00:18:30.750 --> 00:18:32.880
You two are both safe?

00:18:32.880 --> 00:18:36.120
Milo! This thing's main body 
is a coal-eating mantis shrimp.

00:18:36.430 --> 00:18:37.640
It eats bonecoal!

00:18:37.960 --> 00:18:41.070
The fuel Jellyfish tossed 
on it earlier woke it up!

00:18:42.860 --> 00:18:45.450
If this thing runs into 
the Ashio mines now,

00:18:45.450 --> 00:18:48.530
they'll explode, and we won't 
be able to use the railcar!

00:18:46.270 --> 00:18:48.520
<b>Ashio Bonecoal Mountains</b>

00:18:51.140 --> 00:18:52.930
I don't want to die!

00:18:52.930 --> 00:18:55.860
It's no good. I can't handle this 
thing with Jellyfish clinging to me.

00:18:55.860 --> 00:18:57.950
You'll have to do something to make it stop!

00:18:57.950 --> 00:18:59.080
Make it stop?!

00:18:59.080 --> 00:19:01.190
How am I supposed to make it stop?!

00:19:01.190 --> 00:19:03.130
Split open its brow!

00:19:03.130 --> 00:19:06.490
Rattle its brains, 
and even this snail will stop!

00:19:06.490 --> 00:19:08.460
Split its brow with Actagawa's pincers!

00:19:08.720 --> 00:19:12.080
Don't just suddenly ask the 
impossible from a novice crab rider.

00:19:15.710 --> 00:19:17.330
Bisco!

00:19:21.840 --> 00:19:24.990
<i>He told me to make this thing stop.</i>

00:19:25.440 --> 00:19:27.770
<i>If he thinks I can do it...</i>

00:19:27.770 --> 00:19:29.220
<i>Then I'll do it, Bisco.</i>

00:19:30.980 --> 00:19:33.990
Actagawa, that thing's 
weak spot is right here.

00:19:34.530 --> 00:19:35.990
Aim for its brow.

00:19:42.720 --> 00:19:44.320
Go!

00:19:44.320 --> 00:19:46.770
Actagawa!

00:19:51.160 --> 00:19:52.170
Milo!

00:19:56.990 --> 00:19:58.300
Bisco!

00:19:59.150 --> 00:20:00.710
Didn't I tell you?

00:20:00.710 --> 00:20:03.170
You've got a talent for crabs!

00:20:21.580 --> 00:20:22.810
Hey, Bisco.

00:20:23.180 --> 00:20:26.170
Do you always fight such 
incredible opponents?

00:20:26.170 --> 00:20:31.100
Nah, that was definitely my 
first time fighting a temple.

00:20:31.100 --> 00:20:34.380
But I'm sure we'll have to fight 
something even better tomorrow.

00:20:34.380 --> 00:20:37.510
That's just the star we're born under.
 It's a Mushroom Keeper's way of life.

00:20:37.730 --> 00:20:42.020
I think that's just your star,
not one for all Mushroom Keepers.

00:20:43.500 --> 00:20:45.510
This is the entrance to the mines.

00:20:45.510 --> 00:20:49.630
That was a close call. If we had 
let that thing run through here,

00:20:49.630 --> 00:20:52.320
it would've blasted the entire mines to—

00:20:57.140 --> 00:20:58.980
Argh, damn it!

00:20:58.980 --> 00:21:01.770
Is that... Is that even possible?!

00:21:02.560 --> 00:21:04.250
Bisco...

00:21:06.520 --> 00:21:09.500
This doesn't mean we've lost our chance.

00:21:09.500 --> 00:21:11.750
If this way's no good, 
we'll just go a different way.

00:21:12.680 --> 00:21:15.940
Besides, with so many mushrooms 
sprouting on this huge thing,

00:21:15.940 --> 00:21:18.750
the rust will soon be gone in this region.

00:21:19.370 --> 00:21:22.940
The old man would enjoy 
that more than your life.

00:21:31.300 --> 00:21:33.420
Looks like that girl ran off.

00:21:33.420 --> 00:21:35.780
And she took all my money with her.

00:21:35.780 --> 00:21:39.650
I'm going to catch that 
jellyfish and steam her.

00:21:41.020 --> 00:21:43.520
I'm glad I split my money 
between both our wallets.

00:21:44.530 --> 00:21:46.150
Panda-kun
If Akaboshi dies, come 
team up with me, okay?

00:21:44.990 --> 00:21:48.570
<i>Panda-kun, if Akaboshi dies, 
come team up with me, okay?</i>

00:21:46.150 --> 00:21:48.910
Panda-kun
If Akaboshi dies, come 
team up with me, okay?

00:21:49.220 --> 00:21:53.050
She left all kinds of things for us.

00:21:53.050 --> 00:21:55.170
I thought she just took our money.

00:21:55.440 --> 00:21:59.070
Just means she forced us to buy them, 
which is practically the same thing.

00:22:01.320 --> 00:22:04.410
Hey, when did you get Actagawa to let you...

00:22:05.740 --> 00:22:06.920
Those wounds...

00:22:10.800 --> 00:22:12.160
What?

00:22:12.160 --> 00:22:13.560
Nothing.

00:22:36.060 --> 00:22:38.460
I-I'm hungry.

00:22:46.720 --> 00:22:48.470
I-It's a watermelon!

00:22:48.860 --> 00:22:49.980
A watermelon?!

00:22:56.230 --> 00:22:59.230
Hey, wait! That's mine!

00:23:01.310 --> 00:23:03.480
Hey, wait up!

00:23:06.740 --> 00:23:09.610
Come on, brat! Hand it over!

00:23:09.610 --> 00:23:11.750
Bisco, stop that.

00:23:24.920 --> 00:23:37.560
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

00:23:24.920 --> 00:23:37.560
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

00:23:25.750 --> 00:23:27.260
In these hard times,

00:23:27.260 --> 00:23:30.970
children often attack adults and strip
 them of everything in order to survive.

00:23:30.970 --> 00:23:33.840
But this time, they might 
have picked the wrong target.

00:23:34.240 --> 00:23:36.270
Next episode: "Children's Fortress."

00:23:36.270 --> 00:23:39.400
Hey, how much do I get paid 
for this next episode preview?

